{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And He caused a deep sleep to fall upon the human.</b> According to the plain sense, the Holy One, blessed be He, had compassion on the first man, so as not to cause him pain; therefore He caused a deep sleep to fall upon him." "<b>And He slept and took one of his ribs.</b> One of his ribs. Shmuel said: from between his two ribs." "<b>And He closed flesh in its place.</b> It is not written תחתה here, which would mean underneath a thing, but <b>תחתנה</b> is written — meaning under the two of them." "<b>And He closed flesh.</b> Until the creation of the woman, the letter samekh is not written, to teach you that with the coming of the woman came the Satan. Another interpretation: to teach you that the woman is סמוך, close, to her husband. And they raise an objection there: but is it not written ״הסובב את כל ארץ החוילה״ (which contains a samekh)? And they answer: that is written about rivers." "<b>Flesh in its place.</b> He made for him cushions — that is, flesh of the buttocks."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:02:36.514859769Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}